+                /* Left button on the blank desktop belongs to the window
+                 * manager, not to us.
+                 *
+                 * The desktop covers the root window completely, and a window
+                 * manager only ever hears about root clicks by selecting
+                 * ButtonPressMask ON the root -- it does not grab them.  So
+                 * every click on the background stops here, and the WM's root
+                 * menu is unreachable for as long as the desktop runs.
+                 * Handing button 1 back is what keeps it reachable, exactly
+                 * the way show_wm_menu hands back button 3.
+                 *
+                 * forward_pending is set so the RELEASE is forwarded too, by
+                 * the same code that does it for button 3.  Both halves are
+                 * needed: the window manager posts its menu on the press and
+                 * takes a pointer grab for it, and it clears that state on the
+                 * release.  Forwarding only the press leaves it believing a
+                 * button is still held, which makes the NEXT click on the
+                 * desktop behave as part of the menu interaction instead of a
+                 * fresh one.  A release over a menu's f.title entry -- which
+                 * is where ctwm posts the menu, and what the first entry of
+                 * ours is -- leaves the menu up rather than selecting from it.
+                 *
+                 * Rubber-band selection on the blank desktop goes with this;
+                 * that is the trade upstream's FIXME warns about.  Clicking an
+                 * ICON is unaffected: that is handled above, before this
+                 * branch is reached.
+                 */
+                self->forward_pending = TRUE;
+                forward_event_to_rootwin(gtk_widget_get_screen(w), (GdkEvent*)evt);
             }
